        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1281448768,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The spongy pulp of the hard, brown fruit is edible and the fruit is eaten and sold in Madagascar and in eastern Africa; its Swahili name is Mkoma. The flavour has been compared to raisins and raisin bran.",
        "truncated": false
      }
